<title>GREECE: Cut-off price of Greek 10-yr bond auction at 96.03.</title>
<headline>Cut-off price of Greek 10-yr bond auction at 96.03.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following information on Greece's auction of five-, seven- and 10-year bonds was provided by the Bank of Greece.</p>
<p>   Term			     5-yr	  7-yr	 10-yr</p>
<p>   Coupon			   9.2%	  8.9%	  8.8%</p>
<p>   Face value(drachmas)  1.0million	1.0million	1.0million</p>
<p>   Min price accepted	   982,600     962,110     960,300</p>
<p>   Ave price accepted	   986,823.21  969,917.81  969,776.99</p>
<p>   Max price accepted	   994,000     989,000     988,000</p>
<p>   Amount competitive(drs)    75bln	 75bln	 120bln</p>
<p>   Amount non-competitive(drs) 7.5bln	7.5bln	12bln</p>
<p>   Settlement date		 July 17, 1997</p>
<p>--Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
